--- a/docs/cli-reference.rst
+++ b/docs/cli-reference.rst
@@ -25,6 +25,34 @@
 Additional Hints
 ================
 
+Dependency Sources and Entry Points
+----------------------------------
+
+Shiv uses Click 8.1.7. The ``-h``, ``--help``, and ``--halp`` options are equivalent;
+help and version requests exit without installing dependencies or writing an archive.
+
+Use ``--site-packages PATH`` repeatedly to combine existing directories without
+installing dependencies. Directories are processed in command-line order, followed
+by files installed from any supplied pip arguments. Non-conflicting files and
+package metadata are retained; for the same relative path, the later source supplies
+both the contents and permissions. Each path appears only once in the archive.
+Pip arguments not consumed by shiv are forwarded without reordering or rewriting.
+
+An explicit ``--entry-point`` takes precedence over ``--console-script``.
+Console script names are matched exactly in package metadata, with later sources
+taking precedence. A metadata declaration takes precedence over an executable in
+``bin``; without a declaration, a supported executable with the exact requested
+name is required. Executable launchers receive the application's arguments and
+their exit status is returned to the caller.
+
+Archive creation and extraction stage their work before replacing a previous
+result. Failed operations preserve a complete previous result, and subsequent
+invocations recover interrupted staging work automatically.
+
+``shiv-info`` validates the archive before producing text or JSON output. Both
+formats include the stored environment metadata together with the interpreter
+from the shebang and the archive's compression setting.
+
 Choosing a Python Interpreter Path
 ----------------------------------
 
